{
  "type": "output_text",
  "text": {
    "value": "In Apache Shiro 2.0.0 and 2.0.1, the `HashRequest.Builder` class supports a `iterations` parameter, which specifies the number of hash iterations to be performed when computing the final hash result. This parameter is important for increasing the computational effort required to brute-force hashed values, thus improving security.\n\nHere's a relevant Javadoc summary for `HashRequest.Builder`:\n- **iterations:** the number of requested hash iterations to be performed when computing the final Hash result.\n- **Returns:** this Builder instance for method chaining.\n\nYou can also use additional methods such as `addParameter` or set multiple parameters related to hashing as part of the builder process:\n\n```java\nHashRequest request = new HashRequest.Builder()\n    .setAlgorithmName(\"SHA-256\")\n    .setSource(plainTextPassword)\n    .setSalt(salt)\n    .setIterations(1000)\n    .build();\n```\n\nYou can find documentation that describes this as:\n\u003e Parameters: iterations - the number of requested hash iterations to be performed when computing the final Hash result. Returns: this Builder instance for method chaining. See Also: HashRequest.getIterations()【3:1†source】.\n\nThis functionality is consistent across 2.0.0 and 2.0.1, as indicated by release artifacts and javadoc listings for these versions【3:7†source】.\n\nIf you need to check actual method signatures for version 2.0.0 or 2.0.1, you can see the method in the source:\n- `public Builder setIterations(int iterations)`\n\nSo, in summary:\n- `HashRequest.Builder` offers an `iterations` parameter in Shiro 2.0.0 and 2.0.1.\n- There is no reference to `addParameter` directly in the main builder for the hashing process in the context of password hashing, but you may see this in other Shiro configuration elements.\n\nIf you want to set this in Java code, use `setIterations(n)`, and for configuration files you'd use:\n```\nhashService.hashIterations = 1000\n```\nin your shiro.ini, for example【3:6†source】.\n\nLet me know if you need exact code samples for setting up this functionality in your specific Shiro version or context!",
